# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LiveKit (real-time video/audio for interviews)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Self-hosted (docker-compose up livekit):
#   The bundled docker-compose already runs a LiveKit dev server on ws://localhost:7880.
#   In dev mode the token route falls back to devkey/dev-secret automatically — no env needed.
#
# Production self-hosted:
#   1. Remove `--dev` from the livekit service command.
#   2. Mount a livekit.conf with static keys and TLS:
#        LIVEKIT_API_KEY=<your-chosen-key>
#        LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=<random-64-char-hex>
#   3. Add a TURN server (coturn) for NAT traversal — LiveKit docs: https://docs.livekit.io/infra/livekit-server/config/
#
# LiveKit Cloud (free tier — 25 h/month):
#   1. Sign up at https://cloud.livekit.io
#   2. Create a project and copy the API key, secret, and WebSocket URL.
#   3. Set these env vars in your deployment:
LIVEKIT_URL=           # wss://your-project.livekit.cloud
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=       # from LiveKit Cloud dashboard
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=    # from LiveKit Cloud dashboard
#
# TURN/TLS notes for production:
#   - LiveKit Cloud handles TURN + TLS automatically.
#   - Self-hosted: run coturn behind TLS, point livekit.conf to it.
#   - Without TURN, clients behind strict firewalls/NAT will fail to connect.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloudflare Turnstile (bot defense for login/signup/reset)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get keys at https://dash.cloudflare.com/turnstile
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=   # public site key (widget renders in browser)
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=            # secret key (server-side verification only)
# When keys are absent, verification is skipped (fail-open) so deploys
# never lock users out before the admin configures Turnstile.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
